{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Positive.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.grid_barInvariant_iff_unit_or_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.grid_barInvariant_iff_unit_or_half","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.lean#L67-L74","doc":"**The archimedean two-point narrowing (unconditional).** A\ntheta-grid class `u · q̃^ℤ` in `ℝ_{>0}` is bar-invariant iff it is the\nunit class or the half-step class `√q̃ · q̃^ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.barReflect_eq_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.barReflect_eq_div","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The bar reflection on `ℝ_{>0}` is division: `barReflect q̃ s = q̃⁻¹/s`\nat the level of real values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.sqrtPos_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.sqrtPos_sq","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.lean#L55-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.sqrtPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.sqrtPos","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.lean#L49-L53","doc":"The half-step: for positive `v`, the positive square root, with\n`(sqrtPos v)² = v`. Discharges the `hw` hypothesis of the generic\nclassification at `v = q̃`, giving the class of `q̃^{1/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.posReal_two_torsion_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.posReal_two_torsion_free","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.lean#L40-L47","doc":"`ℝ_{>0}` is 2-torsion-free: a positive real square root of `1`\nis `1`. Discharges the `htf` hypothesis of the generic\nclassification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.PosReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.PosReal","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BarReflectionGridSelectionReal.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The multiplicative group of positive reals. ","signatureChunk":0}]}